{"name":"Pale Tidepool","hex":"#c8dcbb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pale","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Light in color.","Having a pallor (a light color, especially due to sickness, shock, fright etc.)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To turn pale; to lose colour.","To become insignificant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pale"},{"term":"tidepool","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rocky pool by the ocean that is filled with seawater left behind by the falling tide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tidepool"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tide pool","blocks":[{"text":"A tide pool or rock pool is a shallow pool of seawater that forms on the rocky intertidal shore. These pools typically range from a few inches to a few feet deep and a few feet across. Many of these pools exist as separate bodies of water only at low tide, as seawater gets trapped when the tide recedes. Tides are caused by the gravitational pull of the sun and moon. A tidal cycle is usually about 25 hours and consists of two high tides and two low tides."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Porto_Covo_February_2009-2.jpg/330px-Porto_Covo_February_2009-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tide_pool","wikidata":"Q1521187"},{"title":"Colorfulness","blocks":[{"text":"Colorfulness, chroma and saturation are attributes of perceived color relating to chromatic intensity. As defined formally by the International Commission on Illumination (CIE) they respectively describe three different aspects of chromatic intensity, but the terms are often used loosely and interchangeably in contexts where these aspects are not clearly distinguished. The precise meanings of the terms vary by what other functions they are dependent on."},{"items":["Colorfulness is the \"attribute of a visual perception according to which the perceived color of an area appears to be more or less chromatic \". The colorfulness evoked by an object depends not only on its spectral reflectance but also on the strength of the illumination, and increases with the latter unless the brightness is very high.","Chroma is the \"colorfulness of an area judged as a proportion of the brightness of a similarly illuminated area that appears white or highly transmitting\". As a result, chroma is mostly only dependent on the spectral properties, and as such is seen to describe the object color. It is how different from a grey of the same lightness such an object color appears to be.","Saturation is the \"colorfulness of an area judged in proportion to its brightness\", which in effect is the perceived freedom from whitishness of the light coming from the area. An object with a given spectral reflectance exhibits approximately constant saturation for all levels of illumination, unless the brightness is very high."]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Brightness_and_colorfulness.png/330px-Brightness_and_colorfulness.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colorfulness","wikidata":"Q27673"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Tide_pools_in_Santa_Cruz_from_Spray-splash_zone_to_low_tide_zone.jpg/500px-Tide_pools_in_Santa_Cruz_from_Spray-splash_zone_to_low_tide_zone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Tide_pools_in_Santa_Cruz_from_Spray-splash_zone_to_low_tide_zone.jpg/1280px-Tide_pools_in_Santa_Cruz_from_Spray-splash_zone_to_low_tide_zone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Tide_pools_in_Santa_Cruz_from_Spray-splash_zone_to_low_tide_zone.jpg/500px-Tide_pools_in_Santa_Cruz_from_Spray-splash_zone_to_low_tide_zone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tide pools in Santa Cruz, California from spray/splash zone to low tide zone","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATide_pools_in_Santa_Cruz_from_Spray-splash_zone_to_low_tide_zone.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Pteropurpura_trialata_is_laying_the_eggs_1.jpg/500px-Pteropurpura_trialata_is_laying_the_eggs_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Pteropurpura_trialata_is_laying_the_eggs_1.jpg/1280px-Pteropurpura_trialata_is_laying_the_eggs_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Pteropurpura_trialata_is_laying_the_eggs_1.jpg/500px-Pteropurpura_trialata_is_laying_the_eggs_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Low tide zone in a tide pool","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APteropurpura_trialata_is_laying_the_eggs_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Tide_pools_in_santa_cruz.jpg/500px-Tide_pools_in_santa_cruz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Tide_pools_in_santa_cruz.jpg/1280px-Tide_pools_in_santa_cruz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Tide_pools_in_santa_cruz.jpg/500px-Tide_pools_in_santa_cruz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The site of a tide pool in Santa Cruz, California showing starfish, sea anemones, and sea sponges.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATide_pools_in_santa_cruz.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/27723-